Godot 4.7.2-stable, Windows: a movement key stays pressed after Korean typing (the walker keeps
walking until the window loses focus). A composition ended by switching the IME off (the text
field lost focus, a click, a closed window) sends WM_IME_ENDCOMPOSITION while the IME is still
marked active, which sets ime_suppress_next_keyup: the next WM_KEYUP of ANY key is then dropped,
typically the release of W/A/S/D. window_set_ime_active(false) now clears that flag and
ime_in_progress. Apply after godot-4.7.2-ime-message-order.patch and build the export templates
(see that patch's header).

diff --git a/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp b/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp
index e821786..d340b0c 100644
--- a/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp
+++ b/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp
@@ -3247,6 +3247,11 @@ void DisplayServerWindows::window_set_ime_active(const bool p_active, DisplaySer
 		ImmAssociateContext(wd.hWnd, (HIMC) nullptr);
 		DestroyCaret();
 		wd.ime_active = false;
+		// A composition ended by switching the IME off (focus left the text field, a click, a closed
+		// window) has no key of its own: its END message must not swallow the next key-up of an
+		// unrelated key (a movement key then stays pressed), and no composition is in progress now.
+		wd.ime_in_progress = false;
+		wd.ime_suppress_next_keyup = false;
 	}
 }
 
